.SH RETURN VALUE
.B \%define_key
returns
.B ERR
if
.bP
no screen has been initialized,
.bP
.I definition
is
.I NULL
and
.I key-code
is nonpositive,
.bP
.I definition
is
.I NULL
and no binding for
.I key-code
exists,
.bP
.I key-code
is nonpositive
and no binding for
.I definition
exists,
.bP
.I definition
is an empty string,
.bP
.I definition
is a prefix of a bound string,
or a bound string is a prefix of
.IR definition ","
or
.bP
insufficient memory is available to bind
.I definition
to
.IR key-code "."
.PP
Otherwise,
.B \%define_key
returns
.BR OK "."
